{#- #620, 10 Sep 2026; rewritten by #830, 28 Sep 2026. The page Close's
    integration directory points at (close.com/integrations/prospektor) and
    the answer to two required fields on their listing form (#9 Marketing URL,
    and "do you promote Close on your website in any way?").

    WHAT THIS PAGE IS FOR, in the operator's words (#830): "much less
    AI-sounding and more humanized. Clear CTAs. 'One month free for Close
    users' should be all over the page. Not 'compare us to all the other
    tools blabla' - just: here is why Prospektor + Close work super well
    together." So the census that #620 led with (39 tools on Close's shelf,
    none writes the email) is gone, and every screen of the page carries the
    offer, one primary action, and one reason the two products fit.

    THE ONE THING THIS PAGE MUST NOT DO: sell whom to chase. Its visitor
    already has a CRM and already believes in it. Everything here is the half
    Close does not have, and where it lands when it is done.

    `/integrations/` rather than `/partners/` (which implies a programme the
    product does not have and would collide with the unbuilt affiliate scheme,
    #87) and rather than `/close/` (a common English word that tells a visitor
    nothing). It mirrors Close's own `close.com/integrations/<name>`, so it
    reads as native from their directory, and it is a namespace that scales to
    HubSpot and Affinity.

    Every claim here is the studio's code, read on 28 Sep 2026, and if one of
    them stops being true this page is wrong, not modest:
      - the one-press connect is the Close OAuth app (#582/#583, live since
        `6aa20f8` on the studio), so no key is pasted;
      - what a push writes is `lib/crm-close.js` (#582, proven in production
        by the operator's own press on 10 Sep): the lead found by domain, its
        contacts, an opportunity whose CONFIDENCE is the fit score, and a
        note that renders; a second press updates by id; an address is added
        beside the ones Close holds and never in place of them;
      - the import is #693's pull: a lead Smart View the owner picks, `name`
        and `url` only, and the companies on it are suppressed from every hunt.

    THE OFFER IS WRITTEN ONLY WHEN THIS BUILD ARMS IT (#622). Every sentence
    that says "free", "30 days" or "$0" sits inside `{% if offer.close %}`, so
    the page cannot promise a month the checkout call would not grant, and the
    dark build is the same page at list price. `test/close.test.js` builds
    both and reads every "N days" against `lib/trial.js`. -#}

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    {%- if offer.close %}
    <span class="tag">{% t %}One month free for Close users{% endt %}</span>
    {%- else %}
    <span class="tag">{% t %}Close integration{% endt %}</span>
    {%- endif %}
    <h1 class="page-h1">{% t %}Prospektor writes the pitch. Close works the deal.{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      {% t %}Prospektor finds the companies worth approaching, names who to talk to
      and writes what you send them, in your voice. One press files all of it in
      Close, where your team already works.{% endt %}
    </p>
    <div class="page-hero-actions">
      {%- if offer.close %}
      <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my free month →{% endt %}</a>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
      {%- endif %}
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="#how">{% t %}How the two fit ↓{% endt %}</a>
    </div>
    {%- if offer.close %}
    <p class="page-hero-note">{% t %}Card on file, nothing charged for 30 days, and one email cancels.{% endt %}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>

<section class="flow" id="how">
  <div class="flow-inner">

    <article class="flowstep">
      <span class="flowstep-n">01</span>
      <div class="flowstep-body">
        <h2>{% t %}Connect Close with one press.{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>
          {% t %}Press Connect Close in your workspace settings and approve it on
          Close's own screen. There is no API key to paste. Prospektor writes to
          the organization you approved and reads nothing out of it unless you
          ask.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p class="flowstep-proof">{% t %}Disconnect from the same panel and the grant is revoked at Close. The steps are in <a href="/help/workspace/">the workspace guide</a>.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="flowstep">
      <span class="flowstep-n">02</span>
      <div class="flowstep-body">
        <h2>{% t %}One press files the whole pitch in Close.{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}Four records, written the way Close models a deal:{% endt %}</p>
        <ul class="pricing-list">
          <li>{% t %}The company as a <strong>lead</strong>, matched on its web domain{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Its named decision-makers as <strong>contacts</strong> of that lead{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}An <strong>opportunity</strong> carrying the fit score as its confidence{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}A <strong>note</strong> holding the fit, the angle, the sources and a link back{% endt %}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="flowstep-proof">{% t %}Push the same pitch again and those records update. Nothing is duplicated.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="flowstep">
      <span class="flowstep-n">03</span>
      <div class="flowstep-body">
        <h2>{% t %}Every line in the note has a source.{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>
          {% t %}The fit score comes with the case for the company and the case
          against it. Each decision-maker carries the source that named them, and
          a name nothing backs is left blank.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p>
          {% t %}Where somebody in your network can open the door, the note says
          who. The link back opens the deck, the one-pager, the cold emails and
          the proposal, drafted in your voice from what has already worked for
          you.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p class="flowstep-proof">{% t %}Addresses already in Close stay as they are. Prospektor adds its own beside them.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="flowstep">
      <span class="flowstep-n">04</span>
      <div class="flowstep-body">
        <h2>{% t %}Your customers in Close teach it who to look for.{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>
          {% t %}Press Import your customers on the Close card and pick the Smart
          View they are in. Prospektor reads each company's name and website,
          never pitches them, and looks for more like them. Nothing else in Close
          is read.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p class="flowstep-proof">{% t %}Only lead views are offered. A contact view is a list of people, and Prospektor has no business holding one.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing pricing-page" id="start">
  <div class="pricing-card">
    {#- Monthly only, deliberately: the offer below is a free month converting to
        a monthly subscription, and a plan switch beside it would be a second
        decision on a page that already has one (the style skill, rule 8). The
        yearly plan is one click away on /pricing/. -#}
    <div class="price-row">
      <span class="price-num">$999</span>
      <span class="price-per">{% t %}/ month · per workspace{% endt %}</span>
    </div>

    {%- if offer.close %}
    {#- #622. Written ONLY when this build's environment arms the offer, so the
        page cannot advertise a trial the checkout call would not grant — and
        the number below is `lib/trial.js`'s constant, which is also the only
        value `CLOSE_TRIAL_DAYS` will accept. test/close.test.js pins the two
        together in both directions. -#}
    <div class="onboard-note">
      <p>{% t %}<strong>First month free for Close users.</strong> Card on file, nothing
        charged for 30 days. Cancel inside them with one email to
        <a href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">hello@prospektor.ai</a> and you are
        never charged.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}

    <ul class="pricing-list">
      <li>{% t %}Unlimited pitch runs: research, scoring and every deliverable{% endt %}</li>
      <li>{% t %}Up to 100 companies in one batch, drafted while the tab is closed{% endt %}</li>
      <li>{% t %}Every colleague on your work-email domain, at no extra cost{% endt %}</li>
      <li>{% t %}Every finished pitch pushed to Close with one press{% endt %}</li>
    </ul>

    {#- The same markup, ids and script as /pricing/'s tile: one field, then
        Stripe. `data-via` is what makes this arrival the Close one — it is on
        the FORM rather than read from the URL, so the offer belongs to the page
        that states it and no query parameter a stranger types can claim it.
        `data-from` sends a cancelled checkout back here instead of to /#pricing. -#}
    <div class="buy" id="buy">
      {%- if offer.close %}
      <a href="{{ '/checkout/' | localize }}" class="btn-cta" id="buyLink">{% t %}Start my free month →{% endt %}</a>
      {%- else %}
      <a href="{{ '/checkout/' | localize }}" class="btn-cta" id="buyLink">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
      {%- endif %}
      <form class="reserve-form buy-form" id="buyForm" data-via="close" data-from="close" hidden novalidate>
        <input class="reserve-input" id="buyEmail" type="email" autocomplete="email"
               placeholder="you@yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your work email{% endt %}">
        <button class="btn-cta" type="submit" id="buyBtn">
          {%- if offer.close %}{% t %}Start my free month · $0 today →{% endt %}{% else %}{% t %}Pay &amp; start · $999/mo →{% endt %}{% endif -%}
        </button>
      </form>
      <input class="reserve-input buy-site" id="buySite" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url"
             placeholder="yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your company website{% endt %}" hidden>
      <p class="reserve-msg is-error" id="buyMsg" hidden></p>
      <p class="buy-note">
        <span id="buyLive" hidden>{% t %}Next stop is Stripe. This address becomes your studio's sign-in, and a work email brings your whole team in with you.{% endt %} </span>
        {%- if offer.close %}{% t %}Nothing is charged for 30 days. After that, money back any month it doesn't earn its keep.{% endt %}{% else %}{% t %}Money back if it doesn't earn its keep, with no fourteen days of hoping you remember to cancel.{% endt %}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{#- defer, like every script this site serves (#137/#170). buy.js looks its
    elements up by id and returns if they are absent, so this page and
    /pricing/ share it without either knowing about the other. No plan.js:
    there is no switch on this page to drive. -#}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/buy.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

<section class="pricing-faq">
  <div class="pricing-faq-inner">
    <h2 class="sec-mid">{% t %}The small print.{% endt %}</h2>
    <dl class="pricing-faq-list">
      {%- if offer.close %}
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>{% t %}How does the free month work?{% endt %}</dt>
        <dd>{% t %}Start here with your work email and a card. Stripe charges
          nothing for 30 days. On day 31 it becomes a normal subscription at
          $999 a month. Cancel before then with one email to
          <a href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">hello@prospektor.ai</a> and
          nothing is charged.{% endt %}</dd>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>{% t %}Who on my team gets in?{% endt %}</dt>
        <dd>{% t %}Everyone on your work-email domain. Pay with your work email and
          every colleague on it signs straight in. There is nothing to count and
          nothing to upgrade.{% endt %}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>{% t %}What does Prospektor read out of Close?{% endt %}</dt>
        <dd>{% t %}Your organization's name when you connect, and the lead and
          contacts a push is about to update. If you import your customers, the
          name and website of each company in the Smart View you picked, and
          nothing else.{% endt %}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>{% t %}What if it doesn't earn its keep?{% endt %}</dt>
        <dd>{% t %}Write to <a href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">hello@prospektor.ai</a>
          and we refund the month. There is no clock on it and no form.{% endt %}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-split">
  <div class="page-split-inner">
    {%- if offer.close %}
    <span class="tag">{% t %}for Close users{% endt %}</span>
    <h2>{% t %}Your first month is free.{% endt %}</h2>
    <p>
      {% t %}Connect Close, run a pitch on a company you want, push it, and see
      what lands. Nothing is charged for 30 days, and one email cancels.{% endt %}
    </p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my free month →{% endt %}</a>
    {%- else %}
    <span class="tag">{% t %}try it{% endt %}</span>
    <h2>{% t %}Free tells you who to chase. Paid gives you what to send.{% endt %}</h2>
    <p>
      {% t %}The scan is free and always will be. Point it at your own site and see who
      it would hunt for you. Everything on this page starts when you do.{% endt %}
    </p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
